     3,
     "\r<br>On Tue, Apr 11, 2017 at 7:52 AM, Bob &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">muen...@tennessee.edu</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi All,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Below is one of the demos from dplyr&#39;s Introduction vignette\r<br>&gt; (<a href=\"https://cran.rstudio.com/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/introduction.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.rstudio.com/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/introduction.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357114132000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0lUbho3pJioqZD0FSlV1Ci\">https://cran.rstudio.com/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/introduction.html</a>).\r<br>&gt; What is the meaning of the question mark?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Thanks,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Bob\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; daily &lt;- group_by(flights, year, month, day)\r<br>&gt; (per_day   &lt;- summarise(daily, flights = n()))\r<br>&gt; #&gt; Source: local data frame [365 x 4]\r<br>&gt; #&gt; Groups: year, month [?]  &lt;=============What does this mean?\r<br>&gt; #&gt;\r<br>&gt; #&gt; # A tibble: 365 x 4\r<br>&gt; #&gt;    year month   day flights\r<br>&gt; #&gt;   &lt;int&gt; &lt;int&gt; &lt;int&gt;   &lt;int&gt;\r<br>&gt; #&gt; 1  2013     1     1     842\r<br>&gt; #&gt; 2  2013     1     2     943\r<br>&gt; #&gt; 3  2013     1     3     914\r<br>&gt; #&gt; 4  2013     1     4     915\r<br>&gt; #&gt; ... with 361 more rows\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
